  "Question": "Three vertices of parallelogram \\(PQRS\\) are \\(P(-3,-2),\\) \\(Q(1,-5),\\) \\(R(9,1)\\) with \\(P\\) and \\(R\\) diagonally opposite. The sum of the coordinates of vertex \\(S\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(13\\)",
    "B": "\\(12\\)",
    "C": "\\(11\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(9\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Opposite sides of a parallelogram have the same length and direction when followed from \\(P\\) to \\(Q\\) and from \\(S\\) to \\(R\\). From \\(P(-3,-2)\\) to \\(Q(1,-5)\\), we move \\(4\\) units right and \\(3\\) units down.\n\nReversing that movement from \\(R\\) gives\n\\[\nS=(9-4,\\,1+3)=(5,4).\n\\]\nThe requested sum is \\(5+4=9\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
